    "title": "Concept: Direct Proportion (y = kx)",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Direct proportion is a relationship where two quantities increase or decrease at the same rate. For example, if one quantity doubles, the other also doubles. Graphically, this results in a straight line that passes through the origin (0,0). The constant <em>k</em> in the equation <strong>y = kx</strong> represents the rate of change or the gradient of the line.</p>",
