    "title": "Identifying the Constant of Proportionality from Graphs",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">The constant of proportionality <em>k</em> can be found by analysing graphs. For direct proportion, the gradient of the straight line (rise over run) equals <em>k</em>. For inverse proportion, the product of corresponding x and y coordinates on the curve is constant and equals <em>k</em>.</p>",
